## 12. Most interesting empirical observation

### [DIRECTLY FROM DATA]

The most striking result is that the previously identified exceptional pattern is **not** the most concentrated subdivision pattern.

The extremal concentration

$$
(6,0,0,0,0,0,0,0,0)
$$

produces

$$
b(T)=3,
$$

whereas the much more balanced pattern

$$
(2,2,2,0,0,0,0,0,0)
$$

is the unique one producing

$$
b(T)=4.
$$

Thus the exceptional \(\Delta_b=2\) behavior occurs at an intermediate subdivision profile rather than at maximum concentration.

### [STRUCTURAL HYPOTHESIS]

This suggests that, for this star core, the interaction among several moderately elongated branches may be more important than simply creating one extremely long branch.

This is an empirical hypothesis only.

